WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:24.416
That was Volcan. Built for Alexa+, it lets a blind or low-vision developer review an AI agent's pull request by voice.

2
00:00:24.416 --> 00:01:21.451
This patch, an inverted admin check, goes to Claude on Amazon Bedrock. Volcan runs on AWS Lambda, with its review state in Amazon DynamoDB. Then a line says how much of the patch the model read.

3
00:01:21.451 --> 00:01:26.885
Amazon Bedrock on the meter, that coverage line, and the model's full answer.

4
00:01:26.885 --> 00:02:00.444
Back on the pull request, request changes stages a review, bound to the head commit Volcan read. Listen.

5
00:02:00.444 --> 00:02:29.727
Nothing leaves Volcan until you confirm. Confirm, and listen.

6
00:02:29.727 --> 00:02:36.645
This build has no GitHub token: the pane shows the exact request, recorded and not sent.

7
00:02:36.645 --> 00:02:45.145
This MCP handshake is a real one with the server under the page. Alexa+ itself has never called Volcan.
